 "region": "worldwide"}}], "screenshots": [{"id": 11328, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/ynxc7wqelxqg9hkwnr94.jpg"}, {"id": 1416683, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/scud4b.jpg"}, {"id": 1416684, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/scud4c.jpg"}, {"id": 1416685, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/scud4d.jpg"}], "slug": "shenmue-ii", "storyline": "In 1987, the teenage martial artist Ryo Hazuki arrives from Japan in Wan Chai, Hong Kong, on the trail of his father's killer, Lan Di, of the criminal Chi You Men organization. He searches for Master Lishao Tao, the only link to the whereabouts of Yuanda Zhu, a martial arts expert who sent Ryo's father a letter warning him of Lan Di's intentions. When Ryo finds Tao, whose real name is Xiuying Hong, she refuses to help, considering his quest for vengeance reckless. The two part ways, but Xiuying continues to monitor Ryo's progress.\n\nRyo encounters Wuying Ren, the wily leader of a street gang. Ren decides to help Ryo after deciding there may be money to be made in Ryo's mysterious phoenix mirror; Lan Di took the second mirror, the dragon mirror, when he killed Ryo's father. Wong, a street boy who admires Ren, and Joy, a free-spirited motorcyclist, assist Ryo in his journey.", "summary": "Yu Suzuki's cinematic masterpiece returns with more spellbinding adventure and an even more immersive world. The epic continues as Ryo Hazuki arrives in Hong Kong on his quest to avenge his father's murder by the warlord Lan Di and unravel the mystery of the Phoenix mirror. Set in Hong Kong, Kowloon, and Guilin, you'll travel through breathtaking scenery, rich with mountainous wilderness, traditional Taoist temples, and stunning tropical landscapes. As you move through massive, highly-detailed 3D worlds, you'll interact with almost every facet of your environment as well as a whole new cast of characters.\n\nOriginally released on Dreamcast in Europe and Japan, this Xbox edition marks the sequel's debut in the US and includes the Shenmue Movie chronicling the first episode in the series.", "themes": [{"id": 1, "name": "Action"}, {"id": 17, "name": "Fantasy"}, {"id": 22, "name": "Historical"}, {"id": 33, "name": "Sandbox"}], "url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/shenmue-ii", "videos": [{"id": 88134, "name": "Gameplay Video", "video_id": "uHFJKtV-RRo", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uHFJKtV-RRo", "title": "Dreamcast Longplay - Shenmue II (part 1 of 8) (OLD)", "thumb": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/uHFJKtV-RRo/hqdefault.jpg"}, {"id": 88135, "name": "Trailer", "video_id": "SM3XxCF3j1g", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SM3XxCF3j1g", "title": "Shenmue 2 Official Xbox Trailer (2002, Sega)", "thumb": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/SM3XxCF3j1g/maxresdefault.jpg"}], "collections": [{"id": 271, "name": "Shenmue"}]}